      "comment_id": "Ugyo9a2ArAFWWzOHQ1d4AaABAg",
      "text": "It actually looks like a pretty good phone , and just looking at its price among all the other main stream phones , it’s still a fair bit cheaper than  the full on flagship models , and appears it is about on the price level give or take a couple of dollars to the main stream big brand base models , Galaxy S25,  iPhone 16, standard pixel, etc .\n  The 3 does look to have some interesting features over and above the common big  brand phones  , at the same time , those big brand base phones do have their own advantages.\n I’m thinking maybe if nothing had run with the snapdragon 8 elite , it might have been a bit more attractive to a lot of buyers even if it cost 100 dollars more than present ….. maybe ?\n Just an observation for my own taste , I think I would have preferred the fancy glyph lights like the previous model than the little circle glyph thing , and another thing about the little circle glyph thing , I could be wrong , but I suspect that glyph button in daily use might be accidentally pressed, bumped  quite often ? But I’m happy to be proven wrong.\n  For me , I think it’s probably a good phone, but I could think of some other phones I’d pick before it .\n But you have to give Nothing some brownie points for throwing caution to the wind and trying something different , apple,samsung, pixel , it’s basically the same stuff every year with just tiny changes.",
